WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.560
- I love that there's a tribute

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.420
to John Mahoney who played your father.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.010
Is that the name of the bar?

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:05.940
- Mahoney's Bar, yeah.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.353
The baby's name is John.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.853
The son, Daphne and Niles', aw, loved him.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:14.783
- And Eddie.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:16.710
Yeah, you have no idea.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:17.940
I have...

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.820
- But yeah, John died a few years back

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.150
and I just thought, well,
we can't do the show again

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.610
without honoring John, we just can't

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.180
and it has to begin with
the fact that John is gone

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.950
and dad's gone, Martin's gone

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.830
and so then I become dad, you know?

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.900
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.842
Okay, my makeup artist will kill me.

00:00:38.842 --> 00:00:40.140
(audience laughing)

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.790
I'm a contagious crier, so...

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:42.660
- Me too.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:43.660
- I'm gonna be fine.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.940
Okay, in Boston though, you're back there.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.470
So do you think any "Cheers"

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:50.587
characters will come in
and out, do you think?

00:00:50.587 --> 00:00:52.800
- No, no.
- No?

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.409
Don't let me down "Cheers" people!

00:00:54.409 --> 00:00:55.680
(audience laughing)

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.710
I was like, "That would
be amazing, just one."

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.153
- The bar is closed.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.170
The bar went out of business.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.220
- For whatever reason.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.770
But I would like to see Diane come back.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.050
Just for one of those reasons,

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.960
of Frazier being able
to put something to bed,

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.320
to end up with a nice thing between them.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.210
- Closure.
- Yeah.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.600
- Yeah, and to kind of
just rediscover how much,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.120
'cause when I first got the role,

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.370
the key to Frazier for me was

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:24.780
that he loved her with his whole heart,

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.240
that he loved with all of his being

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.040
and that actually defined who he is.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.450
He's been that way ever since.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.490
He just goes in
wholeheartedly with everything

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:33.840
and that's what makes him funny.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.363
- Yeah, so witty, oh my gosh.

